                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "In the last year I set out to reverse 10 of Governor Newsom's most harmful policies. We've made significant progress:\n\n1) Gas-Car Ban: My Resolution to reverse the ban passed the House and Senate with bipartisan support.\n\n2) Illegal Health Care: We forced Newsom to end his free Medi-Cal for illegal immigrants policy.\n\n3) Out-of-Control Crime: Our initiative to make crime illegal again, Prop. 36, was passed overwhelmingly by California voters.\n\n4) Homelessness: The Supreme Court ruled in our favor and against Newsom, reversing the 9th Circuit and allowing local communities to clear encampments.\n\n5) High-Speed Rail: The federal government is cutting off funding after the Department of Transportation audit, which we announced in February, found California woefully out of compliance.\n\n6) Sanctuary State: My bill to end sanctuary policies has significant traction, and the combination of executive actions and federal law enforcement has mitigated the sanctuary policy.\n\n7) Water Scarcity: We've secured major funding for the first new significant water storage in California in decades, and we're stopping the diversion of water to the ocean.\n\n8) Catastrophic wildfires: We've passed the Fix Our Forests Act through the House with bipartisan support.\n\n9) Failing Schools: The House just passed the most significant school choice legislation in history, which I sponsored. It is part of the reconciliation bill that will receive a vote in the Senate.\n\n10) Election Chaos: The SAVE Act, a bill I've sponsored to require proof of citizenship to register to vote, has passed the House with bipartisan support.",
